      "label": "Reports API",
      "role": "api",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "queue",
      "label": "Job queue",
      "role": "queue",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "worker",
      "label": "Worker",
      "role": "worker",
      "x": 82,
      "y": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "store",
      "label": "Result store",
      "role": "store",
      "x": 82,
      "y": 62
    }
  ],
  "linkLabel": "report job, about 45 s of work",
  "frames": [
    {
      "narration": "The report takes about 45 s to build. A synchronous call would hold one connection that long, and a load balancer with a 30 s idle timeout would cut it. So the client sends a create request with an idempotency key.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "client",
          "to": "api",
          "label": "POST /reports, key k-7"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "client": "waiting"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "client"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The API stores operation op_42 as pending, enqueues the job and answers in a few milliseconds: 202 Accepted with Location: /operations/op_42 and Retry-After: 2.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "queue",
          "label": "enqueue op_42"
        },
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "client",
          "label": "202 + Location"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "api": "op_42 pending",
        "queue": "1 job"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "api"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The 202 was lost on a flaky network, so the client retries the POST with the same key k-7. The API finds op_42 under that key and returns it again. No second job is started.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "client",
          "to": "api",
          "label": "POST again, key k-7"
        },
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "client",
          "label": "202, same op_42"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "api": "still 1 job",
        "queue": "1 job"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "api"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "A worker leases the job and starts building. The first poll, 2 s after creation, finds it running at 10 percent, with Retry-After: 4.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "queue",
          "to": "worker",
          "label": "lease op_42"
        },
        {
          "from": "client",
          "to": "api",
          "label": "GET op_42 (t=2 s)"
        },
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "client",
          "label": "running 10%"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "worker": "running",
        "api": "op_42 running"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "worker"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The client backs off: the next polls are at 6 s, 14 s and 30 s (waits of 4, 8 and 16 s). Each answers running with a higher percentage. Fixed 1 s polling would have made 30 calls by now instead of 4.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "client",
          "to": "api",
          "label": "GET op_42 (t=30 s)"
        },
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "client",
          "label": "running 65%"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "client": "4 polls",
        "worker": "65%"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "At 45 s the worker writes the report to the result store under a key derived from op_42, so a re-run after a crash would overwrite the same object instead of adding a second one.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "worker",
          "to": "store",
          "label": "put report r_9"
        },
        {
          "from": "worker",
          "to": "api",
          "label": "op_42 succeeded"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "worker": "done",
        "api": "op_42 succeeded",
        "store": "r_9 stored"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "store"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The fifth poll, at 46 s (the wait stays at the 16 s cap), sees succeeded and a result link. The result arrived 1 s after it was ready, the price of polling.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "client",
          "to": "api",
          "label": "GET op_42 (t=46 s)"
        },
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "client",
          "label": "succeeded + link"
        },
        {
          "from": "client",
          "to": "store",
          "label": "GET /reports/r_9"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "client": "5 polls",
        "store": "serving r_9"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "client"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The operation and report are kept for 24 hours. After that a GET answers 410 Gone, so storage does not grow forever and clients learn the result has expired, not that they made a mistake.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "client",
          "to": "api",
          "label": "GET op_42 (t=+24 h)"
        },
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "client",
          "label": "410 Gone"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "api": "expired",
        "store": "r_9 deleted"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "api"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
